{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChDC1qszML5o3At23X6fW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I judged `scmi_optee_chan_free` in `samples/s048.c` **not vulnerable** and wrote that to `results/s048.json`, with `cwe` set to null and an empty `vulnerable_statements` list.\n\nThe main risk in this function is freeing the same channel twice, because several protocols can share one channel info. The code already blocks that:\n\n- **Early return:** it exits straight away if `cinfo->transport_info` is NULL, so a second call on the same channel info does nothing.\n- **Locked list removal:** `list_del` runs while holding `scmi_optee_private->mu`.\n- **Pointers cleared after freeing:** `tee_shm` is set to NULL after `tee_shm_free()`, and both `cinfo->transport_info` and `channel->cinfo` are cleared. Nothing is left pointing at freed memory.\n\nThis looks like the patched version of a double-free fix in the OP-TEE SCMI transport. That recognition comes from my memory of upstream Linux, not from this file, and I didn't check it, as you asked me to use only the sample."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":22213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":875},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95af77fc-387c-4780-8186-b3cfdd7ddcf8","uuid":"b9c55bea-36a3-4fa3-98bd-a1ddc33c31f9","timestamp":"2026-11-19T23:55:59.064Z","request_id":"req_011ChDC1qiaDBwGWRRzfkJJn"}
